.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ic "wattle run"
loads and runs a Wattle script.
Options are read until the first argument that does not begin
with
.Ql "-" .
That argument specifies the script.
All subsequent arguments are passed to the script,
including any that begin with
.Ql "-" .
.Pp
After loading the script,
.Nm wattle
calls its
.Ql "main"
function if it defines one.
The arguments to
.Ql "main"
are the script’s path followed by
.Ar args .
The same arguments are available in the dynamic binding
.Ql "*args*" .
.Pp
With no script and no
.Fl e ,
the command starts a read-eval-print loop (\c\c
.Em REPL )
for interactive evaluation.
.Ic r
is a synonym for
.Cm run .
.Pp
.Cm run
is the subcommand when no other is named.
See
.Xr wattle 1 .
.Pp
An error that a
.Ar script ,
a module loaded with
.Fl l
or code given to
.Fl e
does not handle ends the process with status 1.
.Pp
Options are applied in a fixed order,
regardless of their order on the command line.
The settings
.Fl d ,
.Fl s ,
.Fl r ,
.Fl q
and
.Fl i
are applied first,
followed by
.Fl l ,
then
.Fl e ,
and finally the script.
Each setting applies to every library,
expression and script.
.Fl l
runs before every
.Fl e .
Several
.Fl e
options and several
.Fl l
options run in the order given.
.Pp
.Nm wattle
exits when the script and any tasks it scheduled on the event
loop have finished.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
