.Sh REPL
The REPL reads a line at a time and evaluates each form once
it is complete.
The prompt shows the line number and any open delimiters.
Documentation for a binding is shown with
.Ql "\*(lpdoc symbol\*(rp" ,
and
.Ql "\*(lpdoc\*(rp"
lists the bindings in scope.
.Pp
Prompts are written to standard error,
or to standard output with
.Fl s .
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Xo
.Ev WATTLE_HISTFILE
.Xc
The file used to save the REPL’s history.
Each form submitted at a terminal is appended to this file.
The Up key recalls saved forms in later sessions.
If unset,
history is available only until the REPL exits.
.El
.Pp
.Xr wattle 1
describes
.Ev WATTLE_PREFIX ,
.Ev NO_COLOR ,
.Ev TERM
and
.Ev COLORTERM .
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the REPL:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle
.Ed
.Pp
Run a script with two arguments:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle hello\&.wattle Alice Bob
.Ed
.Pp
Evaluate an expression and print its result:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle -e \(aq\*(lpprint \*(lp+ 1 2 3\*(rp\*(rp\(aq
.Ed
.
